A||||6||GTMike||1.6 rockers||||1||
Z||000000||GTMike||09-25-2001||08:38 PM||||any one done this?  i'm thinking of doing it.  can any one give me a rundown on the process and the parts i will need. <P>also  what type of HP gains can i expect||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||09-25-2001||09:37 PM||||I have the Crane Roller Tip 1.6 rockers. They just bolt on like normal. Now if you mean true rollers, I don't believe anyone makes the metric stud one's anymore so you have to retap the holes in the heads.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dave Gunsul||09-25-2001||10:04 PM||||Cranes Gold Race rockers are made for the Fiero and they are a full roller design.<BR>Formula88 has them on his new 3.4 motor.<BR>They look pretty trick. I didn't use them beacuse I wasn't sure that they'd clear the<BR>valve covers but I guess they do since he used em.<BR>I have a set of 1.52 roller tipped rockers on<BR>my GT but hard to say how much of a difference they made because they were added <BR>with a new motor. They are made by Comp. Cams.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000003||GTMike||09-25-2001||11:04 PM||||terryl  did you notice any gains in power. how much were your roller tips rockers?<P>i'm assuming its a simple install.  just take the valve covers off  unbolt the old ones and bolt the new ones on. <P>did you notice any change in idle?<P>thanks<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Leadfoot||09-26-2001||10:33 AM||||I am changing to the 1.6 over the winter.  From what I am told there should be no complications.  There is a wealth of info on this topic if you do a search in tech. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Boomtastic||09-26-2001||06:59 PM||||I have them too ... very noisey Can't say if they did anything - the engine's been overworked. (bored .060, Crane cam, Accel injectors, etc.) I'm sure that they helped a little bit, since it changes the cam profile.<P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||09-26-2001||07:30 PM||||GT Mike,<P>Well, they were installed with other mods so I can't say if they did or not. They certainly add lift, so I would expect there to be an increase, but how much I can't say.<P>The Gold True rollers (1.5) cleared the Fiero valve covers I installed on my old X-11. At one time Crane made the metric stud versions, but I guess they only make the standards now so you have to re-tap the holes. Does anyone know if Crane is making the metric studs?<P>As for the idle, no, I didn't have any problems with that. BLM's are between 125-131. Idle is stable. So far, the lift doesn't seem to be a big problem but the high overlap cams really throw the MAP off and thus the idle. We're not using that radical of a cam (Blue Racer). I had a Competition Cam in the X-11 that was .440" square and it idled very rough.||||reg||1
